SUMMARY:St Catharine's Political Economy Seminar - Professor Andrés Rodrí
 guez-Pose  -The two geographies of artificial intelligence: AI invention\,
  AI use and regional economic performance in Europe- title tbc
LOCATION:The Ramsden Room\, St Catharine's College
URL:https://talks.cam.ac.uk/talk/index/273737/
CATEGORIES:Politics
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Professor Andrés Rodríguez-Pose\, London School of E
 conomics\nSt Catharine's Political Economy Seminar Series\nTopics: Politic
 s\nDetails: https://talks.cam.ac.uk/talk/index/273737/\nSpeaker: Professor
  Andrés Rodríguez-Pose\n Talk Title: The two geographies of artificial i
 ntelligence: AI invention\, AI use and regional economic performance in Eu
 rope\n Time: 18:00 -19:30 \n Location: Ramsden room\, St Catharine's Colle
 ge \n The seminar series is supported by the Cambridge Political Economy S
 ociety and the Economics and Policy Group at the Cambridge Judge Business 
 School. \n\n Talk Overview: :\n Artificial intelligence (AI) is expected t
 o raise economic performance. Much less is known about where in Europe its
  economic returns land. This article distinguishes between AI invention 
 —the creation of new AI technologies— and AI use —their deployment i
 n production— and asks which of the two is associated with regional econ
 omic performance. AI invention is measured through AI patent applications 
 and AI use through AI labor demand\, the number of AI-skill mentions per 1
 \,000 online job 
END:VEVENT
